cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Shadow Node Theory v2.5.0: Scale-Invariant Satellization and Coupled Orbital Collapse Across Empirical Domains"
abstract: >
  Replication package for Shadow Node Theory v2.5.0 (SNT v2.5.0),
  a formal model of node satellization verified across 721 empirical cases
  reconstructed entirely from verifiable primary sources. The corpus spans
  11 domains and 30 orders of magnitude of temporal scale -- from digital
  platform behavioral cycles (hours) to galactic merger timescales
  (billions of years). The central finding is that institutional friction
  is the dominant predictor of the satellization exponent b
  (Spearman rho = -0.68, p = 2.5e-97, n=714). Version 2.5.0 adds a coupled
  Orbital Collapse layer (ACO-A): an orthogonal collapse axis (Delta), a
  hazard layer h(tau), a three-factor taxonomy of collapse modes
  (friction x trigger x floor/ceiling), and a Principle of Least Friction
  unifying them, with collapse evidence in five domains (finance, history,
  crypto, biology, astronomy) from real data. The v2.4.0 corpus replaced
  the v2.3.1 corpus (502 cases) which contained synthetic values.
  All cases are reproducible from public primary sources via published scripts.
